    "text": "<p>Two blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are placed one over the other on a smooth horizontal surface. The maximum horizontal force that can be applied on lower block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, so that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> move without separation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The coefficient of friction between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0018_ff1f33bbdc15.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 115px;\" /></p>"
